From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] compositor/x11: Assign frame counters only on an actor's views

The compositor calls before_paint for every window on every stage view,
while after_paint and frame_complete only run for actors belonging to the
view. Assigning an X11 sync frame counter on an unrelated view associates
the pending response with a frame which never sends FrameDrawn for that
window. Multi-monitor unminimize tests can then hit the warning about a
frame counter without a frame drawn time.

Match the existing after_paint and presented filtering when assigning the
counter. Keep handle_updates running for every window as before.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/compositor/meta-window-actor-x11.c
+++ b/src/compositor/meta-window-actor-x11.c
@@ -1121,7 +1121,9 @@
 
   handle_updates (actor_x11);
 
-  assign_frame_counter_to_frames (actor_x11);
+  if (g_list_find (clutter_actor_peek_stage_views (CLUTTER_ACTOR (actor)),
+                   stage_view))
+    assign_frame_counter_to_frames (actor_x11);
 }
 
 static void
